  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 195,
      "text": "MEXICO\nintroduced policy uncertainty about the way forward. A new electricity law, however, was approved\nand has replaced auctions by nonmarket-based policies, with regulatory power given to the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 195,
      "end_char": 389,
      "text": "Comisión Federal de Electricidad (CFE), the state-owned electricity company. This has created\nconflicts of interest and disrupted contracts signed under the 2013 reform. Policies should instead\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 389,
      "end_char": 579,
      "text": "aim to encourage private sector participation in the energy sector. Restoring market-oriented\nregulatory frameworks would leverage Mexico’s large and diverse renewable energy resource base.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 579,
      "end_char": 815,
      "text": "It would also provide for cheaper, more reliable, sustainable, and competitive energy supply to the\neconomy and people and secure the needed investment.\n57. Mexico established a climate change mitigation and adaptation agenda early but\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 815,
      "end_char": 996,
      "text": "reducing greenhouse gas emissions will require determined steps, including through\nambitious carbon pricing.14 The expansion of the emission trading system (ETS) in 2023 will be an\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 996,
      "end_char": 1193,
      "text": "important step towards pricing emissions comprehensively. However, questions remain regarding\nthe scalability and parameters of the ETS, which is currently in a pilot phase covering a small number\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1193,
      "end_char": 1394,
      "text": "of large entities. Although these are responsible for around 40 percent of emissions, the ability to\nexpand coverage is not clear. Additionally, the size of the allocated allowances and the absence of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1394,
      "end_char": 1585,
      "text": "legally binding emissions caps mean that the market created by the pilot is limited. Ensuring\nadequate enforcement and monitoring of polluting activity, introducing legally binding emissions\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1585,
      "end_char": 1773,
      "text": "caps, and introducing the planned auction system for allowances are key to making the ETS fully\nfunctional. Further, sectoral measures, such as feebates, public investment in clean energy\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1773,
      "end_char": 2007,
      "text": "infrastructure networks, and regulatory reforms in the energy sector as discussed above could\nenhance the impact of carbon pricing.\nAuthorities’ Views\n58. The authorities pointed to a sharp increase in public investment especially in\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 2007,
      "end_char": 2197,
      "text": "underdeveloped areas, to support growth and reduce regional disparities. They considered\nindustrial policy and strengthening human capital as major priorities to increase productivity. They\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2197,
      "end_char": 2388,
      "text": "agreed on the need to continue advancing the governance agenda and improve the effectiveness of\nthe anti-corruption and AML/CFT framework. They noted that their efforts to improve governance\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2388,
      "end_char": 2582,
      "text": "also included greater reliance on the army to curb crime and the removal of conditionality in\ntransfer programs, the latter to lower the programs’ vulnerability to corruption. They were pleased\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2582,
      "end_char": 2779,
      "text": "that the implementation of the 2019 labor law had already resulted in accelerated resolution of\nlabor disputes. The authorities were seeking to increase labor market formality with the outsourcing\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2779,
      "end_char": 2953,
      "text": "law and tax administration reforms. They considered that a regulatory framework strengthening\ntheir energy state-owned enterprises served the economy better.\nSTAFF APPRAISAL\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2953,
      "end_char": 3136,
      "text": "59. Mexico is well placed to navigate a more challenging, potentially turbulent global\nenvironment. The post-pandemic recovery has been relatively gradual, but domestic inflation has\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3136,
      "end_char": 3255,
      "text": "14 A comprehensive climate mitigation strategy for Mexico is described in IMF WP/21/246.\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 29"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "schema_version": "locator_index_v1",
  "source_id": "MAC-010",
  "source_sha256": "8fac4146590dbe2ed458f7356748f5880d021e03cc4982b1e7efe083d33f622a",
  "locator": "page 34",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 197,
      "text": "MEXICO\naccelerated in line with developments elsewhere. Near-term growth prospects for the U.S. have\nweakened and global financial conditions have tightened as central banks have responded to high\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 197,
      "end_char": 381,
      "text": "inflation, increasing the risks of capital flow reversals in emerging market economies. In this\nenvironment, Mexico will benefit from its very strong macroeconomic policies and policy\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 381,
      "end_char": 564,
      "text": "frameworks but should also prepare contingency plans to react quickly to downside scenarios.\n60. Growth is expected to slow in the near-term and the balance of risks is tilted to the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 564,
      "end_char": 762,
      "text": "downside. After strong outturns in the first half of 2022, growth is projected to decline in the next\nfew quarters, while inflation is expected to gradually fall. More persistent global or domestic\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 762,
      "end_char": 960,
      "text": "inflation, another spike in international oil or food prices, a greater-than-expected tightening of\nglobal financial conditions, or a sharper slowdown in U.S. growth are the main downside risks. On\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 960,
      "end_char": 1112,
      "text": "the upside, an acceleration in nearshoring of production for better access to the North American\nmarket could moderate the impact of lower U.S. growth.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1112,
      "end_char": 1307,
      "text": "61. Tackling high inflation calls for further increases in the policy rate and maintaining it\nthere for some time. With significant uncertainty about the path for inflation in 2023 and important\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1307,
      "end_char": 1511,
      "text": "upside risks, a clearly restrictive policy stance for some time would be appropriate. Further steps in\nusing policy communication as a tool, including further information on the rate path consistent with\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1511,
      "end_char": 1678,
      "text": "Banxico’s inflation forecast, could reinforce the proactive approach to re-anchoring near-term\ninflation expectations and minimizing disruptions in financial markets.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1678,
      "end_char": 1875,
      "text": "62. The envisaged neutral fiscal stance in 2022 and 2023 is appropriate. With the economy\ncurrently operating at close to potential and restoring low and stable inflation a priority, a restrictive\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 1875,
      "end_char": 2045,
      "text": "monetary stance and broadly neutral fiscal stance is an appropriate policy mix.\n63. The untargeted fiscal measures deployed to mitigate the impact of rising living costs\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2045,
      "end_char": 2234,
      "text": "raise efficiency concerns but have supported real incomes. Retail fuel price smoothing has\nreduced cost pressures for the economy but at a sizeable cost to the budget. Shifting to targeted\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2234,
      "end_char": 2416,
      "text": "support could safeguard priority spending and insulate the budget from swings in oil prices.\n64. Fiscal reserves should be restored and the institutional framework for fiscal policy\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2416,
      "end_char": 2615,
      "text": "should be strengthened. Rebuilding the FEIP stabilization fund to around 0.3 to 0.5 percent of GDP\nwould create room for fiscal policy to respond to near-term shocks. In the longer term, more fiscal\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2615,
      "end_char": 2843,
      "text": "policy flexibility to respond to shocks could be achieved through the introduction of an explicit debt\nanchor with narrowly defined escape clauses and a clear mechanism to return to the debt path\nfollowing periods of deviation.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2843,
      "end_char": 3032,
      "text": "65. The floating exchange rate should continue to serve as a shock absorber. The economy\nis expected to remain resilient if downward pressure on the peso materializes, benefiting from deep\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00017",
      "start_char": 3032,
      "end_char": 3230,
      "text": "FX markets and contained FX mismatches in balance sheets. In the event of large shocks to capital\nflows, monetary policy could be used to counter the potential inflationary impact of a weaker peso.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00018",
      "start_char": 3230,
      "end_char": 3352,
      "text": "FX intervention could be considered to mitigate a material worsening of market illiquidity.\n30 INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND"
    }
  ]
}
